# FitzHugh-Nagumo

The purpose of this is to see how the errors scale on a standard nonlinear problem.

```julia
using OrdinaryDiffEq, ParameterizedFunctions, ODEInterface,
      ODEInterfaceDiffEq, LSODA, Sundials, DiffEqDevTools,
      StaticArrays, OrdinaryDiffEqSIMDRK
using OrdinaryDiffEqAdamsBashforthMoulton, OrdinaryDiffEqExtrapolation, OrdinaryDiffEqHighOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqLowOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqVerner
using SciMLLogging
using Plots;
gr()
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "..", "workprecision_table.jl"))

const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ERROR_FLOOR = 1.0e-14
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SIMD_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :simd_rk, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff, :rhs_calls_unavailable]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS = [:sundials, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:sundials, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_LSODA_TAGS = [:lsoda, :multistep, :nonstiff]

f = @ode_def FitzhughNagumo begin
    dv = v - v^3/3 - w + l
    dw = τinv*(v + a - b*w)
end a b τinv l

p = SA[0.7, 0.8, 1 / 12.5, 0.5]
prob = ODEProblem{true, SciMLBase.FullSpecialize}(f, [1.0; 1.0], (0.0, 10.0), p)
probstatic = ODEProblem{false}(f, SA[1.0; 1.0], (0.0, 10.0), p)

abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (6:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (3:10);

sol = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14)
sol2 = solve(probstatic, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14)
test_sol_dense = [sol, sol2]
sol_endpoint = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14, save_everystep = false, dense = false)
sol2_endpoint = solve(probstatic, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14, save_everystep = false, dense = false)
probs = [prob, probstatic]
test_sol = [sol_endpoint, sol2_endpoint];
```

Each sweep requests only the error metrics needed for its measurement with
`error_estimates` and attaches solver metadata tags to the results. The table
with each work-precision figure reports the best endpoint error, that point's
timing, right-hand-side calls, accepted steps, and a computed refinement rate
when the tolerance grid resolves one. Rate calculations exclude errors at or
below `1e-14`, the tolerance used to construct each numerical endpoint reference;
an em dash means that the rate or counter is unavailable or unresolved. Under RHS
calls, the dash in SIMD-RK rows means "RHS-call count not reported: SIMD invocation
unit is ambiguous".

```julia
plot(sol)
```

## Low Order

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode45()) #fails
          Dict(:alg=>dopri5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>BS5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>MER5v2(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SIMD_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>MER6v2(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SIMD_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>RK6v4(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_SIMD_RK_TAGS)]
low_order_setups = setups
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol,
    error_estimates = [:final], save_everystep = false, numruns = 100, maxiters = 1000)
low_order_wp = wp
print_work_table(wp, FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

### Interpolation

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode45()) # fails
          Dict(:alg=>BS5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol_dense, numruns = 100,
    maxiters = 10000, error_estimate = :L2, error_estimates = [:final, :l2, :L2], dense_errors = true)
print_work_table(wp, FITZHUGH_NAGUMO_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

